# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Heavy assets live outside the repo.
#
# The site loads these at runtime; they are deliberately not tracked
# because they run to ~870 MB and two of the Blender files are over
# GitHub's 100 MB hard limit. Copy assets/media and assets/3d into a
# clone (or onto the host) before the gallery and the 3D character
# will appear.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# originals — kept locally, never pushed
assets/media/
assets/1x/*
!assets/1x/favicon.png
portfolio/
assets/3d/*.blend
assets/3d/*.blend1
assets/3d/male*.glb

# assets/web/ holds the re-encoded, deployable versions and IS tracked

# OS / editor noise
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# scratch
_cv_read.pdf
*.log

# the portrait's 5 MB source; assets/portrait.jpg is the 51 KB copy that ships
assets/PIC.png

# unused duplicates of the .jpg maps the material actually loads
assets/3d/diffuse_new.png
assets/3d/normal_new.png

# never loaded — no FBXLoader in the project
assets/3d/butterfly.fbx

# content/ IS tracked. It holds the allocation sheet that tools/allocate.mjs
# turns into js/pages.js — the running order of every page — so a clone
# without it cannot rebuild the site's content. It also holds WORKLOG.md.

# The CV as it arrives from wherever it was written. The copy that ships
# is assets/cv/govind-b-mohan-cv-2026.pdf — same bytes, a filename with
# no spaces in it, and the one SITE.cv points at. Keeping the original
# here is harmless; tracking a second 727 KB copy of it is not.
# Replacing the CV means overwriting the file in assets/cv/ and keeping
# its name, not adding a new one.
content/*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The game — content/Unicorn.
#
# What is tracked is the source: src/, the two authored files in
# dist/ (index.html, style.css), the webpack config and deploy.mjs.
# What is not is the working copy — 59 MB of models, of which the
# game loads 12 — and node_modules. `npm run deploy` writes the
# trimmed, production copy into game/unicorn/, and THAT is what
# ships, the same split as assets/media -> assets/web.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
content/Unicorn/node_modules/
content/Unicorn/blender/
content/Unicorn/dist/*
!content/Unicorn/dist/index.html
!content/Unicorn/dist/style.css

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The avatar studio — content/Fitmint.
#
# What is tracked is the source: AvatarStudio's index.html, src/,
# vendor/, the build in tools/, deploy.mjs and its two README files.
# What is not is the art it is built from and the art it builds:
#
#   Male/        92 MB of source FBX, the artist's GLBs and textures
#   hdri/        the source .exr the lighting is measured from
#   assets/      the build's output — 59 MB of stage-1 intermediate
#                plus the 19 MB payload, which is already in the repo
#                once, as studio/fitmint/
#
# `npm run deploy` writes the shipped copy into studio/fitmint/, and
# THAT is what ships — the same split as assets/media -> assets/web
# and content/Unicorn -> game/unicorn. A clone can serve the site but
# cannot rebuild the studio's assets without the source art.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
content/Fitmint/Male/
content/Fitmint/hdri/
content/Fitmint/AvatarStudio/assets/
content/Fitmint/AvatarStudio/tools/node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent / tooling state.
#
# .impeccable/config.json IS tracked: it is the design detector's
# project config, and the three ignores in it carry written reasons
# that should travel with the repo. Its .local sibling and Claude
# Code's settings do not - the hooks in settings.local.json hold
# absolute C:\Users\... paths that mean nothing on another machine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.impeccable/config.local.json

# The device harness used to inspect phone layouts (see content/NOTES.md).
# Served from the repo root so it is same-origin with the site; never shipped.
_devphone.html
